    "explanation": "Q1 calculates the fraction of users (c4) whose second login occurs exactly one day after their first login, but it joins on TEMP.c4 = A.c4 without filtering for the target date, potentially counting multiple rows per user. Q2 correctly identifies users who logged in on their target date (first_login + 1) by using a LEFT JOIN with the condition table1.c2 = FIRST_LOGIN.TARGET_DATE, ensuring only the target date is considered. The difference arises when a user has multiple logins on dates other than their target date, which Q1 may incorrectly count if those logins happen to match the condition (MIN_DATE + 1) = A.c2 for non-target rows.",
