    "explanation": "Q1 filters rows with c1 BETWEEN '2019-06-28' AND '2019-07-27' (inclusive) before grouping, while Q2 groups all rows first, then filters groups with HAVING c1 > DATE_SUB('2019-07-27', INTERVAL 30 DAY) AND c1 <= '2019-07-27'. The difference arises when there are rows with c1 outside the date range but with c4 values that also appear within the date range. Q1 excludes those rows entirely, while Q2 includes them in the grouping but then filters out the groups, potentially affecting COUNT(DISTINCT c4) for dates within the range if c4 values appear both inside and outside the range.",
